      {
        "id": 84236,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-15T22:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>For Example (from our recent Forum game vs. IL Vigilence vs. accelerated assault: &nbsp;Tachyone played Accelerated assault when she was at 1hp, we chose to have the damage go through to IL before vigilance incapacitated her.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWait, wait, I thought the concensus was that I wouldn't get to do that damage.(Not that it mattered: we took out IL without that damage anyway.)\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Using the new official Order of Operations, having Tachyon resolve Accelerated Assault before Vigilance resolves is a legal action.</p>\n<p>Edit: Also, the Negative Energy Field ruling is kinda obsolete since the Order of Ops. was changed by Christopher in my opinion. I'd suggest reevaluating its usefulness in this context.</p>",
